> How good is NDP Fortran by Microway?  Is it that poor?

I sent email to all companies claiming to sell Fortran compilers for
Linux/Alpha. None responded. From what I have heard from their users,
neither Absoft or NDP are that robust or generate great code. I would
like to test both compilers against the SPEC95 fp benchmarks, if I
could get access to a copy of the compilers. I'm just not enthusiastic
enough about benchmarking to buy a copy of something that has been
reported to me as generating slow code.

> I have a question on this libm thing.  I thought that this libm
> library the most critical thing for floating-point calculation.  But
> not many people mention about this.  We are all lamenting the lack
> of a decent FORTRAN compiler.  Which is the most critical part, the
> compiler or libm?

Both. Some codes are more sensitive to one or the other, but we need
to fix both. None of the SPEC95fp codes use libm that much;
g77-egcs-1.0.3 ranged from 40% slower to 7% faster than Digital
Fortran.

http://www.cs.virginia.edu/~lindahl/spec/

-- g

