I'll confirm #1 and generally speaking, #2.  

>The alphabios doesn't like to read IDE CD-ROMS  

The ARC firmware (Alphabios doesn't show until the 21164 motherboards,
if memory serves...) with most of the Cabriolets out there doesn't
understand the concept of the IDE CD (Because ATAPI didn't exist at
that point in time!).  If you want to install via all IDE hardware (I
**DON'T** reccomend this!  I don't think that the Cabriolet will work
all properly with modern large capacity IDE HDs.) you'll want to
install the latest firmware set, currently downloadable from off of
their FTP archives site.  A word of caution on this: If you are going
to update your firmware, do NOT attempt to do so without making SURE
that you've got clean, uninterrupted power for the duration of the
flash update.  I reccomend a UPS attached to the machine before
attempting this as the flash ROM is wave soldered onto the motherboard
and you may play hell getting the mess fixed- as is with my case.

