Gilles Parent (gilles.parent@univ-fcomte.fr) wrote:

: I have an alpha 21164a on a LX motherboard and I would like
: to install linux with the RedHat 5.1 distribution on cdrom.

: I have the AlphaBIOS 5.62-1a.

: I have configured the BIOS to launch linload.exe by
: filling the "load file" field by CD  \milo\arc\linload.exe.

If you are preparing an automatic boot the best idea is to have
a small FAT partition where linload and milo will live.
Doing that from CD, or floppy, requires a correct media while
booting all the time - which is PITA. Think about reboot after
you lost a power for a few minutes at 2 a.m. and you are not
on UPS.

: But the field "Load Path" MUST be filled by a directory name,

You can put there whatever, the best '\', from whatever partition
as long as milo is called "milo" and is in the same place as linload.
The loader will use its defaults.

: linload
: take this field for "OSLOADFILENAME" too. So it cannot be ok.

But you do not care.

: For instance when I put \lilo in "Load Path" the result is

Error if a directory (watch out!! - directory) does not exist.
So do not do that.  Is that simple.

   Michal




