The SRM software expects certain characteristics if it is going to boot the
device. In fact, it does not accept FAT16 floppies. But this is moot since I
don't think you need to update anything (unless you just feel like it!). Some
systems, and the AlphaStation 200 is one of these, have both the SRM and ARC
consoles in flash at any time - and you just issue commands to switch
between them.

To go from SRM to ARC (or AlphaBIOS):
	>>> set os_type nt
	and after a power-cycle the box will come up in ARC (or AlphaBIOS)

To go from ARC (AlphaBIOS) to SRM you need to wander down the
appropriate menu (mabe : Supplementary >> Setup System >> Machine Specific )
and look for an option that says Switch to OpenVMS or Switch to Digital UNIX
(or maybe even Switch to OSF).

	

