Organization: Customer of Connect.com.au P/L, Sydney, Australia
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha

> It spits out "ATZ" then hangs.  My chat file is identical to the one
>   '' 'ATZ'
>   'OK' 'ATDT5551212'

The problem is your modem is not returning OK from the ATZ command. I had the
same problem. There are two way to fix this:

quick and dirty:
----------------
delete the line with ATZ
change the next line to:
''ATDT95551212

This will fix the problem since you no longer waiting for a return from ATZ.
However, it means you are not resetting the modem.

proper fix:
-----------
Run minicom.
Enter ATZ. You will find you get a newline displayed, but no OK.
Enter AT&F&W. This will reset the modem to the factory defaults. Most modems
have the correct defaults.
Type ATZ. If you get OK returned, your fixed.

I also noticed in the manual pppd line that you use 115200 as the baud rate.
My modems are older ones which will not except this. I had to drop this to
38400. If you already are getting OK returned by ATZ, try this (you may be able
to use 57600). 

Hope this helps,
  Thomas
--
Thomas Behrndt                       behrndt@enternet.com.au



