Kent Kuhler <Kuhlers@mediaone.net> wrote:
: Sounds like your simms are bad.  The messages you are getting are your
: system correcting errors it has detected while reading the simms.  The fact
: that they only register as being 24 MB supports this.  Try testing them in
: another system, or testing other memory in that system.
I can only second this.
One (or both) of your SIMMs seems to be broken.
They have true parity else the machine would not come up at all but I
suspect either one of the RAM chips to be broken or that those SIMMs might
only have one or two bit parity per word (32 bit). The Alpha needs full four
bit per word.
Some SUN machines using PS/2 SIMMs also need parity but only one or two bit
(don't know exactly at the moment) per word.
I had a similiar effect when using a defective SIMM in the Alpha. But the
same SIMM runs fine in a Sparc station (which wants parity too!).
My advice:
  Go and get at least one new SIMM and check this. If you cannot get it to
run properly, change both SIMMs. I do not think that your motherboard is
defective.
CU
  nils

