NNTP-Posting-Date: Tue, 21 Jul 1998 12:11:18 EDT
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha

Hello,

i noticed some messages about this problem, so here what imho the
problem is:

if you dont compile kernel with "Using SRM to boot linux "option set as
Yes (this is  an experimental option and by default is set to NO),  SCSI
bus keeps resetting itself.
when you recompile kernel for some reason again in the future make sure
this option is set to Yes, because it doesn't  save this setting into
kernel config file as "YES" and kept it by default as "NO".

-max




