Odd. Mine saw 32 (though I did have to pass a mem= parameter when I went
to 64MB -- 4x 16MB SIMM). Are you absolutely certain that what you have
are True Parity (aka ECC) 60ns memory? Some folks have reported dealers
selling them "logic parity" memory as true parity.

> I have been told that I probably have a defective mother board, but
> want a second opinion before I stick it in a frame and hang it on the
> wall.

Bad mobo is always a possibility, but try checking the SIMMs you have
and/or trying different ones, if you can, before you give up.

