Hi Keith,

I have the same machine as you have... :-)  and I ran into problems when
compiling new kernel for it after installed RH5.1... Gee, I had to
installed it via FTP through a gateway (my Intel Linux machine over
PPP)... man, it was a chanllenge to get this thing to work, and I think
Linux support on Intel seems a lot better--but, hey, I really enjoyed
learning new stuff. 

Okay, after spending 2 days downloading egcs 1.03a and all the patches
and RH5.1 updates, I tried to compile kernel with the RH5.1 kernel
source, but each time machine will not boot after init SCSI.  Finally,
something hit me and I downloaded a fresh copy of the new Kernel
linux-2.0.35.tar.bz2 and compiled... know what? it worked!  I think that
RH changed Kernel source in some strange way.  So, suggestions to you:

-- download and install egcs 1.0.3a rpms from ftp.redhat.com "contrib"
dir
-- download and install bin-utils from above place
-- download and install the fresh copy of linux 2.0.35 from
www.linuxhq.com

Try if it will work for you.  Oh, recompile and install net-tools v1.4x
if you want get rid off that annoying netstat alignment errors.  One
draw back with 2.0.35, I am having kernel alignment errors with fdisk
and cfdisk.... I can't figure that one out yet.

Hope it helps,

Jack


