masquerading gateway, and saw no differences in gateway performance.  But
for other tasks, such as web server and telnet server, the K5 was faster.
Unfortunately, the K5 died, so I have temporarily replaced it with the
Multia.  Be careful if you use RH 5.1.  I have not been able to get
masquerading to work properly on it.  My AMD worked on RH 5.1 and my Multia
worked on RH 5.0, but no go for 5.1.  Almost every thing is supported better
on the x86 machines.  This alone might be a good enough reason to stick with
the 486


