It looks like Red Hat has a point in supplying buggered 'man' program
as it is not used anyway - at least by some.

Errata do not explain this time shift but documentation on your disk does.
In short, you were asked during an installation if you are using ARC
console time and you answered NO.  Obviously you do use ARC and not
SRM. Change now a contents of /etc/sysconfig/clock; you may also want to
peek in 'man clock' to find out what '-A' flag does and possibly review
how 'clock' is used in /etc/rc.d/rc* files.

