> I installed RH 5.1 [...] on an AlphaStation 500 series.  When it reboots
> after the installation, the screen has:
> device_interrupt: unexpected interrupt 30
> device_interrupt: unexpected interrupt 31
> 
> scrolling continously after the Milo stage.

When installing kernel 2.0.34 on some Miata I saw this a few times,
but only after a "soft" reboot.  My solution was to power-cycle the
machines.  Presumably some PCI registers get left in a confused state
but going back to AlphaBIOS reinitialises them...

AlphaStation's may well be different, though.

Rob.



