Jeff,

From your example below it looks like DU C is faster at floating point. This is
consistent with the complaints I hear from various friends who write simulations
that do a lot of floating point. Not sure how much of that is due to the library
vs the compiled source but one friend tells me he's not impressed with the
register usage for floating point code.

I wonder if anyone has done comparisons using Dhrystone and other commong
non-floating benchmarks like SPECint95.

Sounds like egcs HAIFA is the compiler to use on Linux.

