  i installed RedHat Linux 5.0 (kernel 2.0.30) on Alphastation 200 4/233 which
has SRM boot and use aboot to load os from disk(seems like all systems from
www.onsale.com got same config :-)

here is what i did:

1. boot using following command -> boot dva0 -file vmlinux.gz -flags
"root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1"
2. when you getting to pratitionng part of setup use fdisk and use option "b"
in the fdisk menu which brings you to BSD disklabel format , partion the disk
using this part of fdisk and dont
 forget to reserve first couple blocks of the disk for aboot portion i.e. start
partitioning from block 4 for first partion.
3. check to install Everything option in the menu of packages or check select
packages and in the select menu check mark "aboot" package to get it installed
on the disk
4. when install finished it will reboot the system, boot again from floppy
using following command -> boot dva0 -file vmlinux.gz -flags root=/dev/sda1
(this is my case example)
5. after boot ,login to the system
5.1 cd /sbin
5.2 swriteboot /dev/sda /boot/bootlx
5.3. abootconf /dev/sda 1
5.4 sync and reboot
5.5 at SRM boot prompt set env boot_devdef=dka600, set env boot_osfile
1/vmlinux.gz and set env boot_flags root=/dev/sda1 (all these settings are my
case example, you can have different ID for your drive or different slice on
which your installed your root partion)
6. at SRM prompt type boot and it should load linux from the disk directly

-max




