On 30 Jun 1998, James Hillyerd wrote:

> Could anyone give a rought outline on how to make my AlphaStation 200 4/233
> boot automatically.  Right now the machine pops up the ">>>" prompt and I have
> to put in the boot floppy and type
> 
> boot dva0 -fi vmlinux.gz -fl "root=/dev/sda3"
> 
> I have a 2MB partition /dev/sda1 as some of the howto's/faqs I've looked at
> seem to suggest that.   But I haven't been able to get anything to happen with
> MILO disks/images.

Sure, I can tell you what I did to get mine working (I have the exact same
system booting Linux from SRM).  One exception is that I didn't make a
*partition* for storing aboot, I just made my first partition not start on
the first cylinder, leaving some "dead-zone" space at the beginning of the
drive.

I then used swriteboot /dev/sda /boot/bootlx

Then in the SRM console, I set the environment variables:

boot_file	2/vmlinux.gz (2 is the partition number)
boot_osflags	"root=/dev/sda2" (similar to LILO's append variable)
bootdef_dev	dka0 (the primary SCSI fixed disk)

Then just entering "b" at the SRM prompt will boot the system.

Hope this helps,
-bp
