    IR> I'm going to burn a RedHat 5.1 Alpha CD for Avanti. Can I make
    IR> it bootable or is it possible in i366 only? If it is possible,
    IR> how is the ramdisk.img handled?

<speculation>...so you have been forewarned!

Both ARC and MILO can read ISO-formatted discs.  So put LINLOAD.EXE and
the appropriate MILO and kernel images somewhere on the disc, and you
should be all set for booting from either ARC or MILO.

As for booting from SRM, you'll need to use aboot, which includes a
utility for making ISO-formatted discs bootable (isowriteboot or
something like that).  Be sure to copy the SRM kernel image to the CD!

As for the ramdisk, isn't the CD-ROM supposed to contain a live file
system?  RedHat's FTP site should be already set up for this (it's
used the same way when installing via NFS).

</speculation>

