But No! There's an easier way...
Just do:
    rpm --rebuild <srpm-name>
That will compile the srpm, and re-package it into an installable rpm, and
place that package in /usr/src/redhat/RPMS/$OS

Then just go to that directory, and do rpm -ivh <rpm-name>

            Easy as pie!

