> In the Redhat/Alpha Addendum, Redhat states that it supports both Intel
> and BSD style partitioning.  When I try to install RedHat after
> partitioning with fdisk in BSD mode, or using minlabel, RedHat reports
> that the partition table is corrupt and needs to be initialized.

I had the same problem. Apparently, the Red Hat installation was
"enhanced" to verify the partition table before continuing, and the BSD
table format was forgotten.

My solution was to install to a temporary fdisk-partitioned disk, then
copy the installation to a disk with BSD partitioning, using tar.

Alternatively, RH 5.0 installation works with fdisk in BSD mode.

Randy C.



