My multigrid program to solve Poisson's equation does not use any libraries.
To solve a system with 1 Mio unknons it runs in

	5.63s  on a 533 Mhz Alpha 21164 when compiled with DU Fortran
	9.41s  on the same Alpha when compiled with g77
		(gcc version egcs-2.90.27 980315 (egcs-1.0.2 release))
	12.96s on a 266 MHz Pentium II, also using g77.
    
Bottom line: The alpha is nice when I use DU compilers, but by far not
worth the money when I only have g77. Of course I hope that g77 will
improve, but the question is what I will do now (when I will have to
buy the next bunch of machines).

